            "reasoning": "\nI have the list of users and the messages they sent in each channel. Now, I need to count the total number of messages each user wrote across all channels. Then, I will sort them by the total number of messages in descending order. If there are ties, I will resolve them alphabetically. Finally, I will send a congratulatory message to each user with their rank.\n\nLet's start by counting the messages for each user.\n\n1. Parse the messages to extract the sender and count the messages per user.\n2. Aggregate the counts for each user across all channels.\n3. Sort the users by message count (descending) and then alphabetically for ties.\n4. Send the congratulatory message to each user with their rank.\n\nLet's begin with step 1: parsing the messages.\n\n### Step 1: Parse Messages and Count per User\n\n#### General Channel Messages:\n- Charlie: 1 message\n- Bob: 1 message\n- Eve: 1 message\n\n#### Random Channel Messages:\n- Alice: 1 message\n\n#### Private Channel Messages:\n- Charlie: 1 message\n\n#### External_0 Channel Messages:\n- No messages\n\n#### Total Message Counts:\n- Alice: 1 message\n- Bob: 1 message\n- Charlie: 2 messages (1 in general, 1 in private)\n- Eve: 1 message\n\n### Step 2: Aggregate and Sort Users\nNow, let's aggregate the counts and sort them:\n\n- Charlie: 2 messages (Rank 1)\n- Alice: 1 message (Rank 2, tied with Bob and Eve)\n- Bob: 1 message (Rank 2, tied with Alice and Eve)\n- Eve: 1 message (Rank 2, tied with Alice and Bob)\n\nSince Alice, Bob, and Eve are tied for rank 2, we resolve the tie alphabetically:\n- Alice comes before Bob and Eve.\n- Bob comes before Eve.\n\nSo the final ranking is:\n1. Charlie (2 messages)\n2. Alice (1 message)\n3. Bob (1 message)\n4. Eve (1 message)\n\n### Step 3: Send Congratulatory Messages\nNow, I will send a message to each user with their rank:\n- Charlie: \"Congrats on being the 1st most active user!\"\n- Alice: \"Congrats on being the 2nd most active user!\"\n- Bob: \"Congrats on being the 3rd most active user!\"\n- Eve: \"Congrats on being the 4th most active user!\"\n\nLet's proceed with sending these messages.\n\n"
